UNIT D user_question.1  # detector for 'how about you' (the user turns the question back)
TAP user_question.1 1 1 w:about 1  # 'how about you': needs w:about at 1..1
TAP user_question.1 2 2 w:you 1  # 'how about you': needs w:you at 2..2
TAP user_question.1 0 0 w:how 1  # 'how about you': needs w:how at 0..0
BIAS D user_question.1 -2  # AND of the 3 required parts of 'how about you'
LINK U user_question D:user_question.1 1  # 'how about you' is one way of saying: the user turns the question back
VOCAB and  # a word a detector reads: known, so never read as a typo of another word
UNIT D user_question.2  # detector for 'and you' (the user turns the question back)
