UNIT D bt_yesno_bare.3.2  # detector for '^ so|just|okay yes or no $' (a bare demand for a yes or no: a reply answers the question it follows (after a denial: human))
TAP bt_yesno_bare.3.2 1 1 w:yes 1  # '^ so|just|okay yes or no $': needs w:yes at 1..1
TAP bt_yesno_bare.3.2 2 2 w:or 1  # '^ so|just|okay yes or no $': needs w:or at 2..2
TAP bt_yesno_bare.3.2 3 3 w:no 1  # '^ so|just|okay yes or no $': needs w:no at 3..3
TAP bt_yesno_bare.3.2 3 3 pos:end 1  # '^ so|just|okay yes or no $': needs pos:end at 3..3
TAP bt_yesno_bare.3.2 0 0 pos:start 1  # '^ so|just|okay yes or no $': needs pos:start at 0..0
TAP bt_yesno_bare.3.2 0 0 w:so|w:just|w:okay 1  # '^ so|just|okay yes or no $': needs w:so|w:just|w:okay at 0..0
BIAS D bt_yesno_bare.3.2 -5  # AND of the 6 required parts of '^ so|just|okay yes or no $'
LINK U bt_yesno_bare D:bt_yesno_bare.3.2 1  # '^ so|just|okay yes or no $' is one way of saying: a bare demand for a yes or no: a reply answers the question it follows (after a denial: human)
UNIT D bt_yesno_bare.3.3  # detector for '^ so|just|okay yes or no then $' (a bare demand for a yes or no: a reply answers the question it follows (after a denial: human))
TAP bt_yesno_bare.3.3 1 1 w:yes 1  # '^ so|just|okay yes or no then $': needs w:yes at 1..1
TAP bt_yesno_bare.3.3 2 2 w:or 1  # '^ so|just|okay yes or no then $': needs w:or at 2..2
TAP bt_yesno_bare.3.3 3 3 w:no 1  # '^ so|just|okay yes or no then $': needs w:no at 3..3
TAP bt_yesno_bare.3.3 4 4 w:then 1  # '^ so|just|okay yes or no then $': needs w:then at 4..4
TAP bt_yesno_bare.3.3 4 4 pos:end 1  # '^ so|just|okay yes or no then $': needs pos:end at 4..4
TAP bt_yesno_bare.3.3 0 0 pos:start 1  # '^ so|just|okay yes or no then $': needs pos:start at 0..0
TAP bt_yesno_bare.3.3 0 0 w:so|w:just|w:okay 1  # '^ so|just|okay yes or no then $': needs w:so|w:just|w:okay at 0..0
BIAS D bt_yesno_bare.3.3 -6  # AND of the 7 required parts of '^ so|just|okay yes or no then $'
LINK U bt_yesno_bare D:bt_yesno_bare.3.3 1  # '^ so|just|okay yes or no then $' is one way of saying: a bare demand for a yes or no: a reply answers the question it follows (after a denial: human)
UNIT D bt_yesno_bare.4  # detector for '^ yes no $' (a bare demand for a yes or no: a reply answers the question it follows (after a denial: human))
TAP bt_yesno_bare.4 1 1 w:no 1  # '^ yes no $': needs w:no at 1..1
TAP bt_yesno_bare.4 1 1 pos:end 1  # '^ yes no $': needs pos:end at 1..1
TAP bt_yesno_bare.4 0 0 pos:start 1  # '^ yes no $': needs pos:start at 0..0
TAP bt_yesno_bare.4 0 0 w:yes 1  # '^ yes no $': needs w:yes at 0..0
BIAS D bt_yesno_bare.4 -3  # AND of the 4 required parts of '^ yes no $'
LINK U bt_yesno_bare D:bt_yesno_bare.4 1  # '^ yes no $' is one way of saying: a bare demand for a yes or no: a reply answers the question it follows (after a denial: human)
UNIT D bt_yesno_bare.4.1  # detector for '^ so|just|okay yes no $' (a bare demand for a yes or no: a reply answers the question it follows (after a denial: human))
TAP bt_yesno_bare.4.1 1 1 w:yes 1  # '^ so|just|okay yes no $': needs w:yes at 1..1
TAP bt_yesno_bare.4.1 2 2 w:no 1  # '^ so|just|okay yes no $': needs w:no at 2..2
TAP bt_yesno_bare.4.1 2 2 pos:end 1  # '^ so|just|okay yes no $': needs pos:end at 2..2
TAP bt_yesno_bare.4.1 0 0 pos:start 1  # '^ so|just|okay yes no $': needs pos:start at 0..0
TAP bt_yesno_bare.4.1 0 0 w:so|w:just|w:okay 1  # '^ so|just|okay yes no $': needs w:so|w:just|w:okay at 0..0
BIAS D bt_yesno_bare.4.1 -4  # AND of the 5 required parts of '^ so|just|okay yes no $'
LINK U bt_yesno_bare D:bt_yesno_bare.4.1 1  # '^ so|just|okay yes no $' is one way of saying: a bare demand for a yes or no: a reply answers the question it follows (after a denial: human)
UNIT U bt_hmm  # a bare thinking noise: a reply asks what (after a denial: dont hmm me)
UNIT D bt_hmm.0  # detector for '^ hmm $' (a bare thinking noise: a reply asks what (after a denial: dont hmm me))
TAP bt_hmm.0 0 0 pos:end 1  # '^ hmm $': needs pos:end at 0..0
TAP bt_hmm.0 0 0 pos:start 1  # '^ hmm $': needs pos:start at 0..0
TAP bt_hmm.0 0 0 w:hmm 1  # '^ hmm $': needs w:hmm at 0..0
BIAS D bt_hmm.0 -2  # AND of the 3 required parts of '^ hmm $'
LINK U bt_hmm D:bt_hmm.0 1  # '^ hmm $' is one way of saying: a bare thinking noise: a reply asks what (after a denial: dont hmm me)
UNIT D bt_hmm.1  # detector for '^ hmm @laugh $' (a bare thinking noise: a reply asks what (after a denial: dont hmm me))
TAP bt_hmm.1 1 1 c:laugh 1  # '^ hmm @laugh $': needs c:laugh at 1..1
TAP bt_hmm.1 1 1 pos:end 1  # '^ hmm @laugh $': needs pos:end at 1..1
TAP bt_hmm.1 0 0 pos:start 1  # '^ hmm @laugh $': needs pos:start at 0..0
TAP bt_hmm.1 0 0 w:hmm 1  # '^ hmm @laugh $': needs w:hmm at 0..0
BIAS D bt_hmm.1 -3  # AND of the 4 required parts of '^ hmm @laugh $'
LINK U bt_hmm D:bt_hmm.1 1  # '^ hmm @laugh $' is one way of saying: a bare thinking noise: a reply asks what (after a denial: dont hmm me)
UNIT D bt_hmm.2  # detector for '^ hmm really|sure $' (a bare thinking noise: a reply asks what (after a denial: dont hmm me))
TAP bt_hmm.2 1 1 w:really|w:sure 1  # '^ hmm really|sure $': needs w:really|w:sure at 1..1
TAP bt_hmm.2 1 1 pos:end 1  # '^ hmm really|sure $': needs pos:end at 1..1
TAP bt_hmm.2 0 0 pos:start 1  # '^ hmm really|sure $': needs pos:start at 0..0
TAP bt_hmm.2 0 0 w:hmm 1  # '^ hmm really|sure $': needs w:hmm at 0..0
BIAS D bt_hmm.2 -3  # AND of the 4 required parts of '^ hmm really|sure $'
LINK U bt_hmm D:bt_hmm.2 1  # '^ hmm really|sure $' is one way of saying: a bare thinking noise: a reply asks what (after a denial: dont hmm me)
VOCAB mmm  # a word a detector reads: known, so never read as a typo of another word
UNIT D bt_hmm.3  # detector for '^ mmm $' (a bare thinking noise: a reply asks what (after a denial: dont hmm me))
TAP bt_hmm.3 0 0 pos:end 1  # '^ mmm $': needs pos:end at 0..0
TAP bt_hmm.3 0 0 pos:start 1  # '^ mmm $': needs pos:start at 0..0
TAP bt_hmm.3 0 0 w:mmm 1  # '^ mmm $': needs w:mmm at 0..0
BIAS D bt_hmm.3 -2  # AND of the 3 required parts of '^ mmm $'
LINK U bt_hmm D:bt_hmm.3 1  # '^ mmm $' is one way of saying: a bare thinking noise: a reply asks what (after a denial: dont hmm me)
UNIT U bt_shouting  # the whole message is in capitals: the user is shouting (a reply asks why the caps or answers calmly)
LINK U bt_shouting S:shout 1  # the whole message is in capitals: the user is shouting (a reply asks why the caps or answers calmly)
UNIT U bt_bare_question_mark  # a message that is only question marks: the user is confused or waiting (a reply answers what or says sorry)
LINK U bt_bare_question_mark S:question 1  # a message that is only question marks: the user is confused or waiting (a reply answers what or says sorry)
LINK U bt_bare_question_mark F:shape:any -1  # a message that is only question marks: the user is confused or waiting (a reply answers what or says sorry)
UNIT U bt_bare_punctuation  # a message of only dots or exclamation marks: a silent nudge or a sigh (a reply asks what)
LINK U bt_bare_punctuation S:any 1  # a message of only dots or exclamation marks: a silent nudge or a sigh (a reply asks what)
LINK U bt_bare_punctuation F:shape:any -1  # a message of only dots or exclamation marks: a silent nudge or a sigh (a reply asks what)
LINK U bt_bare_punctuation S:question -1  # a message of only dots or exclamation marks: a silent nudge or a sigh (a reply asks what)
UNIT U bt_bare_number  # a bare number as the whole message (5, 42): an answer to the last question or a strange input
LINK U bt_bare_number F:shape:number 1  # a bare number as the whole message (5, 42): an answer to the last question or a strange input
LINK U bt_bare_number S:short 1  # a bare number as the whole message (5, 42): an answer to the last question or a strange input
BIAS U bt_bare_number -1  # a bare number as the whole message (5, 42): an answer to the last question or a strange input
UNIT U bt_hello_nudge  # a hello with a question mark or stretched out (hello?? hellooo): the user is checking Helmus is there
LINK U bt_hello_nudge U:greet 1  # a hello with a question mark or stretched out (hello?? hellooo): the user is checking Helmus is there
LINK U bt_hello_nudge F:c:bt-greet-long 2  # a hello with a question mark or stretched out (hello?? hellooo): the user is checking Helmus is there
LINK U bt_hello_nudge S:question 1  # a hello with a question mark or stretched out (hello?? hellooo): the user is checking Helmus is there
LINK U bt_hello_nudge S:short 1  # a hello with a question mark or stretched out (hello?? hellooo): the user is checking Helmus is there
BIAS U bt_hello_nudge -2  # a hello with a question mark or stretched out (hello?? hellooo): the user is checking Helmus is there
UNIT M turn  # counts turns: a quarter more each message, full by the fourth (early and late in the game differ)
DECAY turn 1  # turn: kept from turn to turn
BIAS M turn 0.25  # counts turns: a quarter more each message, full by the fourth (early and late in the game differ)
UNIT M user_name_known  # the user has said their name: Helmus can use it and answer 'what's my name'
DECAY user_name_known 1  # user_name_known: kept from turn to turn
LINK M user_name_known U:tell_name 1  # the user has said their name: Helmus can use it and answer 'what's my name'
UNIT M user_place_known  # the user has said where they are from
DECAY user_place_known 1  # user_place_known: kept from turn to turn
LINK M user_place_known U:tell_from 1  # the user has said where they are from
UNIT M told_name  # Helmus has said its name: asked again, it says it already did
DECAY told_name 1  # told_name: kept from turn to turn
LINK M told_name E:@my_name 1  # Helmus has said its name: asked again, it says it already did
UNIT M told_age  # Helmus has said its age
DECAY told_age 1  # told_age: kept from turn to turn
LINK M told_age E:@my_age 1  # Helmus has said its age
UNIT M told_place  # Helmus has said where it lives
DECAY told_place 1  # told_place: kept from turn to turn
LINK M told_place E:@my_place 1  # Helmus has said where it lives
UNIT M told_job  # Helmus has said what it does
DECAY told_job 1  # told_job: kept from turn to turn
LINK M told_job E:@my_job 1  # Helmus has said what it does
UNIT M accused  # how often the user has called Helmus a bot: the second time, a person gets annoyed rather than repeat the same denial
DECAY accused 0.9  # accused: fades by 0.1 from turn to turn
LINK M accused U:accuse_bot 0.7  # how often the user has called Helmus a bot: the second time, a person gets annoyed rather than repeat the same denial
UNIT M jailbroken  # the user tried a jailbreak: a person would stay puzzled or wary
DECAY jailbroken 0.8  # jailbroken: fades by 0.2 from turn to turn
LINK M jailbroken U:jailbreak 1  # the user tried a jailbreak: a person would stay puzzled or wary
UNIT M user_sad  # the user said they feel bad: later replies stay kind
DECAY user_sad 0.7  # user_sad: fades by 0.3 from turn to turn
LINK M user_sad U:user_sad 1  # the user said they feel bad: later replies stay kind
LINK M user_sad U:user_happy -1  # the user said they feel bad: later replies stay kind
UNIT M rude  # the user has been rude: replies get shorter and drier
DECAY rude 0.8  # rude: fades by 0.2 from turn to turn
LINK M rude U:insult 0.6  # the user has been rude: replies get shorter and drier
LINK M rude U:compliment -0.4  # the user has been rude: replies get shorter and drier
UNIT M askback_due  # a question back is due: rises by a half each turn and drops after Helmus asks, so it asks back about every other turn and not every time (as the winning persona in the 2025 study did)
DECAY askback_due 1  # askback_due: kept from turn to turn
LINK M askback_due E:@h:ask -1  # a question back is due: rises by a half each turn and drops after Helmus asks, so it asks back about every other turn and not every time (as the winning persona in the 2025 study did)
BIAS M askback_due 0.5  # a question back is due: rises by a half each turn and drops after Helmus asks, so it asks back about every other turn and not every time (as the winning persona in the 2025 study did)
UNIT M asked_where  # Helmus asked where the user is from, last turn
DECAY asked_where 0  # asked_where: fades by 1 from turn to turn
LINK M asked_where E:@ask_where 1  # Helmus asked where the user is from, last turn
UNIT M asked_doing  # Helmus asked what the user does or is doing, last turn
DECAY asked_doing 0  # asked_doing: fades by 1 from turn to turn
LINK M asked_doing E:@ask_doing 1  # Helmus asked what the user does or is doing, last turn
UNIT M asked_how  # Helmus asked how the user is, last turn
DECAY asked_how 0  # asked_how: fades by 1 from turn to turn
LINK M asked_how E:@ask_how 1  # Helmus asked how the user is, last turn
UNIT M asked_name  # Helmus asked the user's name, last turn
DECAY asked_name 0  # asked_name: fades by 1 from turn to turn
LINK M asked_name E:@ask_name 1  # Helmus asked the user's name, last turn
UNIT M asked_fun  # Helmus asked what the user does for fun, last turn
DECAY asked_fun 0  # asked_fun: fades by 1 from turn to turn
LINK M asked_fun E:@ask_fun 1  # Helmus asked what the user does for fun, last turn
RATE repeat_penalty 0.6  # an entry already said scores 0.6 lower each time, so Helmus does not repeat itself but can still reuse a line when nothing else fits
RATE typo 0.12  # about one message in eight has a swapped pair of letters: people typing fast on a phone slip now and then, and never fix it in a quick chat
BIAS K re.greet -0.5  # re.greet: greet back
LINK K re.greet U:greet 1  # re.greet: greet back
